g smartness is **Rule 14**, which requires being both nice and green. Since Bob is not nice, he cannot be smart.\n   - No other rules provide an alternative pathway to being smart (e.g., no rule states \"kind and green implies smart\").\n\n4. **Conclusion on Furrieness:**\n   - Without being smart, Bob cannot satisfy the conditions for being quiet (Rule 8). Since quietness is the only route to furrieness (Rule 12), Bob cannot be furry.\n   - The conditional in **Rule 15** (\"If Bob is kind and not green, then Bob is furry\") is irrelevant because Bob is green.\n\n**Final Answer:** The statement \"Bob is furry\" is **False (B)**.",
