rmation includes the first statement, then Charlie is young is given, so unless that leads to a contradiction, which it doesn\'t, then it\'s true. So the answer is A. But maybe the problem is a trick question where the first statement is part of the context, so it\'s a given, so the answer is A. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the question is testing whether the initial statement is necessarily true given the rest, but in that case, the first statement is part of the premises, so we must take it as true unless there\'s a contradiction. Since there isn\'t, the answer is A. \n\nHmm, I think that\'s solid. So I\'ll go with A) True.\n'] 31%|███       | 186/600 [5:37:31<11:02:40, 96.04s/it] 
