n1. Erin is red (given).\n2. Therefore, Erin is nice (from rule12: red → nice).\n3. Since Erin is red and nice, rule15 says she must be cold.\n4. Cold → rough (rule14), so Erin is rough.\n5. Rough and nice → round (rule13), so Erin is round.\n6. Round → green (rule16), so Erin is green.\n\nEvery step follows necessarily. Therefore, the conclusion must be true. Hence, the answer is A) True.\n'] 34%|███▍      | 205/600 [6:11:01<9:45:15, 88.90s/it]
