would have to be round. Since he is not round, he **cannot be rough**.\n   - Thus, **Harry is not rough**, making the statement **true**.\n\n### Determining Roundness:\n- There is no rule forcing Harry to be round. The rules only impose conditions *if* he is round (e.g., must be cold and rough), but they do not require him to be round. Harry\u2019s attributes (young, nice, furry) do not necessitate roundness through any rule.\n\n### Conclusion:\nSince Harry could be either round (making the statement false) or not round (making the statement true), **the truth value is undetermined**. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n**C) Unknown**",
