t** (directly stated).\n\n2. **Infer Furriness**: \n   - Since Charlie is **quiet**, the rule \"All quiet things are furry\" (fact 13) applies. Thus, **Charlie is furry**.\n\n3. **Apply Rule 19 (Furry + Blue \u2192 White)**: \n   - Charlie is **furry** (from step 2) and **blue** (given). Rule 19 states: \"If something is furry and blue, it is white.\" Therefore, **Charlie must be white**.\n\n4. **Apply Rule 15 (White \u2192 Cold)**: \n   - Since Charlie is **white**, the rule \"White things are cold\" (fact 15) applies. Thus, **Charlie must be cold**.\n\n5. **Check for Contradictions**:\n   - No rules conflict with this conclusion. For instance:\n     - Rule 14 (\"If Charlie is cold, then Charlie is young\") is satisfied because being cold implies youth (via the chain: cold \u2192 white \u2192 young via other rules, but even without that, the conclusion only requires coldness).\n     - Charlie being young is consistent with other rules (e.g., \"All young things are nice\").\n\n6. **Conclusion**:\n   - The logical chain **blue + quiet \u2192 furry \u2192 white \u2192 cold** is unbroken and valid. Thus, **Charlie must be cold**.\n\n**Answer**: A) True",
