n   - From \"All young people are furry\" (statement 10), Charlie is **furry** (consistent with given data).\n\n2. **Contradiction if Charlie is Round**:\n   - If Charlie were round, the rule \"If someone is round and nice, they are not young\" (statement 12) would apply.\n   - Since Charlie is **nice** and assumed **round**, this rule forces Charlie to be **not young**.\n   - However, Charlie is already **young** (from being smart). This creates a contradiction (young and not young simultaneously).\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - The assumption that Charlie is round leads to a contradiction. Therefore, **Charlie cannot be round**.\n   - The statement \"Charlie is round\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer**: B) False",
