t, that\'s a bit ambiguous. Does it mean things that are both red and green must be furry? Yes. So if something is both red and green, then it must be furry. Since Fiona, if she is red and green, that would require her to be furry, which she is. So that\'s okay.\n\nAlternatively, maybe someone could argue that being green and blue might not require being red, but according to the steps, she must be round, so red.\n\nAlternatively, maybe someone might think that rule6 (if round → red) overrides any other attributes? But yes, the rules are all supposed to be true.\n\nTherefore, I think the answer is A) True. So I\'ll go with that.\n'] 50%|█████     | 301/600 [9:20:59<10:31:10, 126.66s/it]
