ait, maybe Gary is not furry because of some contradiction?\n\nSuppose Gary is furry. Then he must be white (statement 10). To be furry, he must be white and smart (statement 8). Since he is smart (from big), that\'s okay. But to be white, he must be quiet and cold (since that\'s the only way). Therefore, if he is furry, then he must be cold. But we don\'t know if he is cold, so that\'s possible but not necessary. So the statement could be true or false, so it\'s unknown.\n\nAlternatively, could there be a reason Gary cannot be furry?\n\nSuppose he is not cold, so not white, so not furry. Or he is cold, so white and smart, so furry. Since his coldness is unknown, both possibilities exist. Therefore, the answer is unknown.\n\nHence the correct option is C.\n'] 60%|█████▉    | 359/600 [11:10:24<6:27:16, 96.42s/it]
