her the bear visits the mouse. The conditionals give us a lot of derived conclusions but don\'t directly address the bear\'s visit to the mouse. The only mention of the bear\'s visits is that it doesn\'t visit the tiger (fact8).\n\nTherefore, since there\'s no information or conditional that requires or prohibits the bear from visiting the mouse, the answer should be unknown (C).\n\nWait, but wait a second. Let me double-check if any of the conditionals might have an indirect effect.\n\nSuppose we assume that the bear does visit the mouse. Then, by conditional20, the bear must be kind. Now, if the bear is kind, and if the bear is also cold, then by conditional6, it would be big. But the bear\'s temperature isn\'t stated. The bald eagle is cold, but the bear\'s isn\'t. So we can\'t assume the bear is cold. Therefore, being kind doesn\'t necessarily make the bear big unless it\'s cold, which we don\'t know.\n\nAlternatively, if the bear is not kind, then it can\'t visit the mouse (since visiting the mouse requires being kind via conditional20). Wait, no. Wait, conditional20 is "If something visits the mouse then it is kind". The contrapositive is "If something is not kind, then it does not visit the mouse". So, if the bear is not kind, then it cannot visit the mouse. But if the bear is kind, it can visit, but there\'s no rule forcing it to visit. So the bear\'s visitation to the mouse depends on whether it\'s kind, but we don\'t know the bear\'s kindness.\n\nTherefore, since we can\'t determine if the bear is kind (and hence can or cannot visit the mouse), the statement is unknown.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there\'s another angle. Let\'s think of all entities that visit the mouse:\n\nWe know the bald eagle visits the mouse (from conditional3 and fact4). Are there others?\n\nIf the mouse visits itself, but that\'s not stated. The tiger doesn\'t visit the mouse unless stated. The bear\'s visit is the question.\n\nSo the only known visitor to the mouse is the bald eagle. The others are unknown.\n\nThus, the bear visiting the mouse is not determined by the given information. Therefore, the answer should be unknown (C).\n'] 62%|██████▏   | 373/600 [11:43:23<10:17:27, 163.21s/it]
