n\n3. **Analysis of Possibilities for Anne\u2019s Color:**  \n   - **If Anne is white:**  \n     This is consistent with her being rough (satisfies Statement 11). No contradictions arise.  \n   - **If Anne is not white:**  \n     - She cannot be red and rough (due to Statement 13, which would force her to be white).  \n     - She could be a different color (e.g., blue), as no rule restricts rough people to only red or white.  \n\n4. **No Mandatory Link to Whiteness:**  \n   - There is no rule forcing all rough individuals to be white. The problem does not state that all colors must be red or white, leaving room for other colors.  \n\n5. **Conclusion:**  \n   Since Anne could be white or another color without violating any given rules, her color remains **unknown**.  \n\n**Answer:** C) Unknown",
