n   - The rabbit is cold (Fact 4), so it must **chase the rabbit** (itself).\n\n2. **Rule 2**: \"If something chases the rabbit, it eats the bear.\"  \n   - Since the rabbit chases the rabbit (from Rule 4), the rabbit must **eat the bear**.\n\n3. **No Contradictions**:  \n   - The conclusion that the rabbit eats the bear does not violate any other rules or facts.  \n   - For example, Rule 9 (\"If something eats the bear, it chases the squirrel\") would require the rabbit to chase the squirrel, but this is allowed as there is no rule prohibiting it.  \n   - Other rules (e.g., Rule 5, Rule 8) do not negate the conclusion because their conditions (e.g., \"the bear visits the squirrel\") are not met.\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe logical chain (Rule 4 \u2192 Rule 2) forces the rabbit to eat the bear. Thus, the statement is **true**.\n\n**Answer:** A) True",
