gh.\n\nThus, if Charlie were red, he must be rough, but he can\'t be rough, so Charlie can\'t be red. Therefore, the statement "Charlie is not red" is necessarily true. So the answer is A) True.\n\nHmm, but wait another angle: Let\'s see if Charlie could be red through another path. Suppose someone else\'s attributes affect him? Probably not. All the rules are about the properties of individual things. So I think the logic holds.\n'] 87%|████████▋ | 524/600 [16:29:17<2:58:12, 140.70s/it]
