oes not need the lion (only the lion needs the squirrel, per statement 7).  \n     - **Statement 19** (\"If someone eats the mouse and the mouse is nice, then the mouse does not need the bald eagle\") does not conflict because the mouse\u2019s needs are not tied to the bald eagle (statement 9 says the mouse needs the lion).  \n\nNo contradictions arise from the squirrel being nice. Thus, the statement **\"The squirrel is nice\" is true**.\n\n**Answer:** A) True",
